D('in which',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The archive describes the year in which the bridge was completed.','档案记载了这座桥竣工的年份。')],mistakes:[m('The archive lists the year in which was the bridge completed.','The archive lists the year in which the bridge was completed.','in which 引导嵌入式关系从句时用陈述语序，不倒装 was the bridge。')],quiz:[q('in which',1,1,'“The room in which the meeting took place” identifies?','the room where it took place','the meeting’s duration','the people who attended','in which 可引出说明所在地点的关系从句。'),q('in which',2,1,'Which shorter word often replaces in which when referring to a place?','where','when','whose','where 可替代地点义的 in which。'),q('in which',3,1,'Choose the correct embedded clause: “the year in which ___.”','the law changed','did the law change','changed the law did','关系从句采用陈述语序 the law changed。'),q('in which',4,1,'“The report in which the figures appear” means the figures appear?','inside that report','before the report was written','because the report was lost','in which 在此指数字出现于该报告中。')]});
D('in-between',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The shop stocks an in-between size for customers who find small too tight and medium too loose.','这家商店备有中间尺码，适合觉得小码太紧、中码太松的顾客。')],mistakes:[m('The tailor offered an in-between size that was smaller than both the small and medium sizes.','The tailor offered a smaller size that was smaller than both the small and medium sizes.','夹在两者之间的尺码不可能比两者都小；中性 smaller 与描述相符。')],quiz:[q('in-between',1,1,'An in-between option lies?','between two other options','outside the available choices entirely','at the beginning of a sequence','in-between 表示处于两者之间。'),q('in-between',2,1,'A person between childhood and adulthood may be at an in-between?','stage','invoice','engine','in-between stage 是中间阶段。'),q('in-between',3,1,'Which item could be an in-between size?','a shoe size between two standard sizes','a size identical to the smallest size','a size that is not measured at all','中间码介于两个标准尺码之间。'),q('in-between',4,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','an in-between answer','an in-betweenly answer','an between-in answer','in-between 在这里作复合形容词修饰 answer。')]});
D('inaccurate',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The weather app gave an inaccurate forecast and predicted sun during the storm.','天气应用的预报不准确，在暴风雨期间预测会有阳光。')],mistakes:[m('The scale was inaccurate but gave the exact same weight as the certified balance every time.','The scale was accurate and gave the same weight as the certified balance every time.','次次与认证天平读数相同表明测量准确，和 inaccurate 矛盾。')],quiz:[q('inaccurate',1,1,'An inaccurate map may?','show roads in the wrong locations','match every verified landmark','provide exact directions every time','inaccurate 指不准确、有错误。'),q('inaccurate',2,1,'Which report is inaccurate?','one that states a meeting began at 9 when it began at 10','one that records the verified start time correctly','one that is clearly labeled as a draft','把会议时间写错的报告是不准确的。'),q('inaccurate',3,1,'Choose the noun that names the quality of being inaccurate.','inaccuracy','accuracy','accurately','inaccuracy 是 inaccurate 对应的名词。'),q('inaccurate',4,1,'A measurement is inaccurate if it?','differs from the true value','repeats the verified true value','has no number assigned to it','测量值偏离真实值才是不准确。')]});
D('inactive',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The old account is inactive because no one has signed in for two years.','这个旧账户处于未活跃状态，因为两年来无人登录。')],mistakes:[m('The volcano is inactive and has erupted three times this week.','The volcano is active and has erupted three times this week.','本周多次喷发说明火山正在活动；active 才与事实一致。')],quiz:[q('inactive',1,1,'An inactive bank account is one that?','is not currently being used','receives dozens of transactions daily','has just been opened and is busy','inactive 表示当前不活动或未被使用。'),q('inactive',2,1,'An inactive volcano is generally?','not erupting at present','erupting continuously now','a volcano that has no mountain','inactive 可指当前不喷发的火山。'),q('inactive',3,1,'Which person might be described as inactive in a club?','a member who no longer takes part','a member organizing every event','a member attending all weekly meetings','不再参与俱乐部活动的成员可称 inactive。'),q('inactive',4,1,'Choose the opposite adjective.','active','idle','dormant','active 是 inactive 的反义词。')]});
D('inactivity',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'Long periods of inactivity during the winter left the machine stiff.','机器冬天长期闲置，导致运转不灵活。')],mistakes:[m('Regular movement reduced inactivity, so the patient became more inactive each day.','Regular movement reduced inactivity, so the patient became more active each day.','活动减少了不活动状态，结果应是更 active，而不是更 inactive。')],quiz:[q('inactivity',1,1,'A period of inactivity is a period when someone?','does little or no activity','works continuously without rest','moves faster than usual','inactivity 指缺乏活动或不活跃的状态。'),q('inactivity',2,1,'Long-term physical inactivity may refer to?','not getting enough bodily movement','training for a marathon daily','recovering from a single sprint','该词可指长期缺少身体活动。'),q('inactivity',3,1,'Which form is the noun? “The machine’s ___ caused a delay.”','inactivity','inactive','inactively','空格作主语中心名词，应填 inactivity。'),q('inactivity',4,1,'The report links inactivity to a lack of use. Here inactivity is?','the state of not operating or being active','a sudden rise in production','a person’s high level of effort','机器没有运行、没有被使用就是 inactivity。')]});
D('inadequate',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The emergency shelter had inadequate blankets for the freezing night.','应急避难所的毯子不足以应付寒冷的夜晚。')],mistakes:[m('The water supply was inadequate, with enough clean water for every household and a large reserve.','The water supply was adequate, with enough clean water for every household and a large reserve.','每户有足够洁净水且有储备，说明供应充足而非 inadequate。')],quiz:[q('inadequate',1,1,'An inadequate amount of evidence is?','not enough to support the claim','more than the claim could ever need','evidence that proves every detail','inadequate 表示数量或程度不足。'),q('inadequate',2,1,'Which response is inadequate for a five-hour hike?','one small bottle of water for a group of ten','enough water for each hiker','a tested emergency supply','少量水无法满足十人长途徒步需要。'),q('inadequate',3,1,'A worker with inadequate training?','has not been trained enough for the job','has mastered every required skill','has no assigned role or job','培训不足意味着尚未达到工作要求。'),q('inadequate',4,1,'Choose the closest opposite.','sufficient','deficient','insufficient','sufficient 意为足够，与 inadequate 相反。')]});
D('inaugural',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The newly elected mayor delivered her inaugural address from the steps of city hall.','新当选的市长在市政厅台阶上发表了就职演说。')],mistakes:[m('The retiring mayor gave an inaugural speech after serving in the same office for thirty years.','The retiring mayor gave a farewell speech after serving in the same office for thirty years.','卸任时发表的是告别演说；inaugural 指就职或首次举行。')],quiz:[q('inaugural',1,1,'An inaugural address is usually given?','at the start of someone’s term in office','after the person retires','before an election campaign begins','inaugural 可指就职时发表的演说。'),q('inaugural',2,1,'A museum holds its inaugural exhibition. This is likely?','its first exhibition','its final exhibition after closing','an exhibition repeated every week for years','inaugural 也可表示首次举办的。'),q('inaugural',3,1,'Which event would most naturally be called inaugural?','the first annual lecture in a new series','the tenth lecture in an established series','a private meeting with no speaker','新系列的首次讲座是 inaugural event。'),q('inaugural',4,1,'Which adjective is closest to inaugural in “inaugural season”?','first','annual','final','inaugural season 是首个赛季。')]});
D('inaugurate',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The city inaugurated a night-bus service to connect the hospital with the suburbs.','市里开通了一项夜间公交服务，连接医院和郊区。'),ex(3,'Residents gathered as the new science center was inaugurated.','新科学中心举行落成仪式时，居民们聚集在现场。')],mistakes:[m('The president was inaugurated last year, so the ceremony will put her into office for the first time tomorrow.','The president was inaugurated last year, so tomorrow’s ceremony will mark her anniversary in office.','已经宣誓就任后，明天的活动不能再次让她首次就职。')],quiz:[q('inaugurate',1,1,'To inaugurate a president is to?','formally install the president in office','remove the president from office','publish the president’s memoir','inaugurate 的政治义是举行就职仪式、使正式就任。'),q('inaugurate',2,2,'A city inaugurates a new night-bus service when it?','officially starts the service','cancels the service permanently','tests a bus without opening the route','inaugurate 可表示开创或正式开始一种服务。'),q('inaugurate',3,3,'A building was inaugurated on Friday. The building was?','officially opened in a ceremony','closed for demolition','designed but never completed','建筑义是举行落成或启用仪式。'),q('inaugurate',4,1,'Which sentence uses the office-related sense?','The new governor was inaugurated before the crowd.','The library was inaugurated with a ribbon cutting.','The policy was inaugurated after a pilot program.','新州长就任对应举行就职仪式这一义项。')]});
D('inborn',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'Her inborn patience helps her remain calm with anxious clients.','她天生的耐心帮助她在面对焦虑的客户时保持冷静。')],mistakes:[m('His inborn language skill was acquired only after a six-month course as an adult.','His language skill was acquired only after a six-month course as an adult.','成年后通过课程获得的技能是后天习得的，不是出生时已有的 inborn 特质。')],quiz:[q('inborn',1,1,'An inborn ability is?','present from birth','learned only through a recent course','borrowed from another person','inborn 的核心义是先天具备。'),q('inborn',2,2,'A person’s inborn love of music is described as?','a natural part of their character','a preference forced on them yesterday','a song they have never heard','该义强调构成性格的内在特质。'),q('inborn',3,1,'Which is closest in meaning to inborn?','innate','acquired','temporary','innate 与 inborn 都指先天的。'),q('inborn',4,1,'Which phrase uses inborn naturally?','an inborn talent for rhythm','an inborn lesson learned last week','an inborn passport issued yesterday','talent for rhythm 可描述天生才能。')]});
D('inbuilt',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The smoke detector has an inbuilt battery that keeps it working during a power cut.','烟雾探测器内置电池，停电时仍能继续工作。')],mistakes:[m('The camera has an inbuilt lens that was detached and stored in a separate case.','The camera has a removable lens that was detached and stored in a separate case.','已经拆下并另行存放的镜头不是内置组件；removable 符合描述。')],quiz:[q('inbuilt',1,1,'An inbuilt safety feature is?','included as part of the design','added only after the device is dismantled','kept in a separate building','inbuilt 指设计时装在内部或本身具备的。'),q('inbuilt',2,1,'A phone with inbuilt navigation can?','navigate without a separate navigation unit','navigate only after its screen is removed','never determine its location','内置导航是设备本身具有的功能。'),q('inbuilt',3,1,'Which phrase is a natural synonym in this context?','built-in protection','borrowed protection','external protection only','built-in 与 inbuilt 都表示内置的。'),q('inbuilt',4,1,'Choose the sentence that fits inbuilt.','The alarm has an inbuilt backup battery.','The alarm’s battery is inbuilt in a box across town.','The alarm inbuilted a backup battery.','backup battery 是报警器自身设计内置的部件。')]});
D('incentive',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'Employees who meet the safety target receive a cash incentive.','达到安全目标的员工会得到现金奖励。'),ex(3,'Lower fares gave commuters an incentive to leave their cars at home.','较低的票价促使通勤者把车留在家里。')],mistakes:[m('The bonus was an incentive to meet the target, but it was offered to discourage anyone from meeting it.','The bonus was an incentive to meet the target, and it was offered to encourage people to meet it.','奖励作为 incentive 的作用是鼓励目标行为，不能同时说它用来阻止该行为。')],quiz:[q('incentive',1,1,'A flexible schedule can be an incentive to join a company because it?','encourages people to apply','forces every applicant to leave','measures the company’s office size','incentive 是促使某人采取行动的激励因素。'),q('incentive',2,2,'A cash incentive offered for safe driving is?','a reward intended to encourage safer behavior','a fine imposed for a traffic violation','a refund unrelated to driving','以现金奖励鼓励安全驾驶，是奖励措施义。'),q('incentive',3,3,'There is little incentive to save when interest rates are low. Here incentive means?','a motive or reason to save','a guaranteed payment for saving','a law forbidding savings','此处指促使储蓄的动机或理由。'),q('incentive',4,1,'Which phrase is standard?','an incentive to invest','an incentive for invest','an incentive of investing','常见结构是 an incentive to do something。')]});
D('inch',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The climber would not give an inch during the negotiation.','谈判期间，登山者寸步不让。'),ex(3,'As the traffic cleared, the queue inched toward the bridge.','交通逐渐畅通后，车队一点点向桥边移动。')],mistakes:[m('The board is three inch thick, according to the ruler.','The board is three inches thick, according to the ruler.','表示长度数值三时，单位 inch 应用复数 inches。')],quiz:[q('inch',1,1,'One inch is equal to?','2.54 centimetres','10 centimetres','one metre','英寸是长度单位，1 inch 合2.54厘米。'),q('inch',2,2,'“She would not give an inch” means she?','refused to yield even slightly','gave away a full ruler','measured the room carefully','give an inch 是让步一点点，否定形式表示寸步不让。'),q('inch',3,3,'If traffic inches forward, it?','moves very slowly in small amounts','travels rapidly without stopping','turns around and goes backward','动词 inch 表示缓慢、一点点地移动。'),q('inch',4,1,'Choose the correct measurement.','The shelf is six inches deep.','The shelf is six inch deep.','The shelf is six inchs deep.','数值大于一时用复数 inches。')]});
D('incidence',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The study examined the incidence of errors in copied records.','这项研究考察了抄录记录中错误的发生情况。'),ex(3,'The incidence of the new fee falls mainly on small retailers.','这项新费用的负担主要落在小零售商身上。')],mistakes:[m('The incidence of the illness rose, meaning fewer people developed it each year.','The incidence of the illness fell, meaning fewer people developed it each year.','疾病发生率上升意味着发生得更多而非更少，应改为 fell。')],quiz:[q('incidence',1,1,'A high incidence of flu in winter refers to?','a high rate at which flu cases occur','the number of hospital rooms','the length of each flu symptom','发生率义关注疾病或事件出现的频率。'),q('incidence',2,2,'Researchers studied the incidence of recording errors. They studied?','how often the errors occurred','how expensive the recorder was','which employee bought the recorder','sense 2 指某事发生、出现的情况。'),q('incidence',3,3,'If the incidence of a tax falls on consumers, consumers?','bear its economic burden','collect the tax from the government','are exempt from the tax','税负 incidence 指负担最终落在哪些人身上。'),q('incidence',4,1,'Which topic most naturally uses incidence to mean a rate?','the incidence of measles over time','the color of a single desk','the address of a clinic','疾病 incidence 常用于统计其发病率。')]});
D('incident',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The spilled coffee was a minor incident, and the meeting continued.','咖啡洒出来只是个小插曲，会议继续进行。'),ex(3,'The two patrols met after a border incident near the river.','河边发生边境冲突后，两支巡逻队碰了面。'),ex(4,'Some risks are incident to working at sea.','有些风险是海上工作所固有的。')],mistakes:[m('The border incident was purely incidental to the dispute and involved an armed exchange between patrols.','The border incident was a serious clash in the dispute and involved an armed exchange between patrols.','武装巡逻冲突是严重事件；incident 不能在此说成次要附带之事。')],quiz:[q('incident',1,1,'Police are investigating a serious incident. They are investigating?','an unusual or troubling event','a routine timetable','the police station’s address','incident 常指值得调查的事件或事故。'),q('incident',2,2,'A minor incident at lunch is likely?','a small episode with limited consequences','a war between two nations','a formal adjective meaning accidental','minor incident 指影响较小的小插曲。'),q('incident',3,3,'A border incident between two countries may involve?','a hostile clash or confrontation','a shared birthday party','a routine weather report','国家间语境中 incident 可指冲突或摩擦。'),q('incident',4,4,'“Risks incident to the job” are risks?','naturally associated with the job','unrelated to the job','that have already been eliminated','正式用法 incident to 表示伴随、与某事相关。')]});
D('incidental',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The grant covered incidental costs such as local bus fares and photocopies.','这笔拨款还支付了当地公交费、复印费等附带开支。')],mistakes:[m('The contract lists the main fee as incidental and treats the small photocopy charge as the most important cost.','The contract lists the main fee as the principal cost and treats the small photocopy charge as incidental.','主要费用不是次要附带费用；复印费才是附带的小额开支。')],quiz:[q('incidental',1,1,'Incidental costs are usually?','secondary expenses connected with the main activity','the central purpose of the activity','costs that are never paid','incidental costs 指附带产生的次要费用。'),q('incidental',2,1,'A brief mention of an unrelated detail is incidental if it is?','not the main point','the whole subject of the discussion','required to complete the main task','incidental 可形容顺带提及、非重点的内容。'),q('incidental',3,1,'Which item could be an incidental expense on a work trip?','a small local transit fare','the employee’s entire annual salary','the company’s main building','行程中的小额公交费是附带支出。'),q('incidental',4,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','incidental expenses','incidentally expenses','incidental expenseful','incidental 是形容词，可修饰 expenses。')]});
D('incline',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'Her careful explanation inclined the panel to approve the trial.','她细致的解释使评审小组倾向于批准这项试验。'),ex(3,'The narrow path inclines sharply toward the stream.','这条狭窄小路急剧向溪流方向倾斜。'),ex(4,'A steep incline led from the valley to the lookout.','一段陡坡从山谷通向观景台。')],mistakes:[m('He has an incline to daydream whenever the lecture gets technical.','He has an inclination to daydream whenever the lecture gets technical.','表示性格倾向的名词通常是 inclination；incline 作名词主要指斜坡，源词条所列此结构不自然。')],quiz:[q('incline',1,1,'“I incline to agree with the proposal” means?','I tend to agree with it','I have already signed it','I am physically standing on it','动词 incline to 可表示倾向于某种看法。'),q('incline',2,2,'The evidence inclined the jury to reconsider. It?','made the jury more willing to reconsider','prevented the jury from hearing evidence','forced the jury to leave the room','及物 incline 可表示使某人愿意做某事。'),q('incline',3,3,'The road inclines to the left. The road?','slopes toward the left','ends immediately at the left','is perfectly level','动词 incline 描述道路向一侧倾斜。'),q('incline',4,4,'A steep incline is?','a sharply sloping stretch of ground','a level indoor floor','a formal speech','名词 incline 的常见义是斜坡。')]});
D('inclined',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'After hearing both proposals, I am inclined to support the less costly one.','听取两个方案后，我倾向于支持成本较低的那个。')],mistakes:[m('She is inclined to help, but she refuses every request and never offers assistance.','She is disinclined to help, and she refuses every request and never offers assistance.','反复拒绝且从不帮忙表示不愿意；disinclined 与行为相符。')],quiz:[q('inclined',1,1,'“I am inclined to agree” means?','I am somewhat likely or willing to agree','I have been physically pushed to the floor','I have already proved the claim false','be inclined to 表示倾向于、愿意做某事。'),q('inclined',2,1,'Which completion is correct? They are inclined ___ the safer route.','to choose','choosing','for choose','be inclined to 后接动词原形。'),q('inclined',3,1,'A person inclined to worry is?','likely to worry','unable to feel worry','always forced to leave','inclined to worry 表示容易或倾向于担心。'),q('inclined',4,1,'Which word is closest here? “He is inclined to volunteer.”','prone','certainly forbidden','unrelated','prone to 可表示倾向于某行为。')]});
D('include',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'The invitation includes guests’ partners in the head count.','邀请函将来宾的伴侣也计入人数。'),ex(3,'Please include the delivery fee when you compare the final prices.','比较最终价格时，请把运费也算进去。')],mistakes:[m('The entry fee includes a meal, but visitors must pay extra because the meal is already included.','The entry fee includes a meal, so visitors do not pay extra for it.','既然门票已包含餐食，就不能又说必须另付费用。')],quiz:[q('include',1,1,'The price includes breakfast. Breakfast is?','part of the price','available only at an extra charge','excluded from the offer','include 可表示某物作为整体的一部分被包含。'),q('include',2,2,'“Please include Jo in the email chain” asks you to?','add Jo to the group of recipients','remove Jo from the project','send the email only to yourself','include someone in a group 是把某人列入其中。'),q('include',3,3,'When estimating a trip, remember to include the fuel cost. You should?','count the fuel cost as part of the total','exclude the fuel cost from every calculation','pay the fuel seller twice','include the cost 表示把费用算入总额。'),q('include',4,1,'Which sentence is grammatically correct?','The package includes two replacement filters.','The package is include two filters.','The package includes of two filters.','include 是及物动词，后直接接所包含的内容。')]});
D('income',{extraExamples:[ex(2,'Tourism is now the island’s largest source of income.','旅游业如今是这座岛最大的收入来源。'),ex(1,'Her monthly income comes from teaching and freelance editing.','她每月的收入来自教学和自由编辑工作。')],mistakes:[m('The shop’s income fell, so it received more money from sales than ever before.','The shop’s income rose, so it received more money from sales than ever before.','销售收入比以往更多表示 income rose，而不是 fell。')],quiz:[q('income',1,1,'A person’s income is?','money they receive from work or investments','the total cost of their groceries','a loan they must repay immediately','income 是从工作或投资等来源获得的钱。'),q('income',2,2,'National income refers to money received by?','a country’s economy as a whole','one tourist visiting the country','a single household’s grocery bill','national income 指国家层面的收益或收入。'),q('income',3,1,'Which phrase means a person earns relatively little?','a low income','an income tax return','a high-income bracket','low income 是低收入的自然搭配。'),q('income',4,1,'Choose the correct sentence.','Rental income helped pay for the repairs.','The income were helped pay the repairs.','Rental incomes helped paying for repaired.','income 可作不可数名词表示租金收入。')]});
D('inconsistency',{extraExamples:[ex(1,'The reviewer found an inconsistency between the table and the paragraph describing the sample size.','审阅者发现表格与描述样本量的段落之间存在不一致。')],mistakes:[m('The two accounts match in every detail, revealing a clear inconsistency between them.','The two accounts match in every detail, revealing no inconsistency between them.','两份记录完全一致意味着没有 inconsistency；加 no 是最小修正。')],quiz:[q('inconsistency',1,1,'An inconsistency between two records means they?','do not agree with each other','match in every detail','were written at the same time','inconsistency 指彼此不一致或缺少协调。'),q('inconsistency',2,1,'A report contains an inconsistency if one page says 12 and another says 21 for the same total. The report?','gives conflicting information','repeats the same correct figure','contains no numbers','同一总数出现冲突数字，就是内容不一致。'),q('inconsistency',3,1,'Which noun is closest in meaning?','discrepancy','consistency','agreement','discrepancy 可指差异或不一致。'),q('inconsistency',4,1,'Choose the plural form. The auditors noted several ___.','inconsistencies','inconsistencys','inconsistent','inconsistency 的复数拼写为 inconsistencies。')]});
